            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter aspiration of atheroma prolapsing through saphenous vein graft stents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>258-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endoluminal stenting has often become the percutaneous treatment of choice for older vein grafts. We report a case of successful stenting of a degenerated vein graft that was complicated by prolapse of atheroma through the stents leading to ischemia that was successfully reversed by catheter aspiration of the prolapsed atheroma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
